"app.py"

Main application code. User input ni process chesi fire detection result ni display cheyadaniki use chestundi.

"forest_fires.csv"

Forest-fire related dataset/data information kosam use chese CSV file.

"forest_fire_model.pkl"

Trained machine-learning model file.

"index.html"

Web interface structure kosam use chese HTML file.

"style.css"

Application/web page design and styling kosam.

"script.js"

Web page interactions kosam JavaScript file.

"requirements.txt"

Project run cheyadaniki required Python libraries list.

---

🚨 Detection Results

System possible ga following results ni provide chestundi:

🌳 Normal Forest

Forest Image
     ↓
No Fire Detected
     ↓
Normal Status

💨 Smoke Detected

Forest Image
     ↓
Smoke Detected
     ↓
Early Warning

🔥 Fire Detected

Forest Image
     ↓
Fire Detected
     ↓
High Confidence
     ↓
Forest Fire Alert

Detection result lo Fire/Smoke, bounding box, confidence score, detection status and alert lantivi display cheyagaladu.

---

🚀 Installation & Running

1. Repository Clone

git clone https://github.com/madhuriyeepuri098/Forest-Fire-Detection-System.git

2. Project Folder ki vellandi

cd Forest-Fire-Detection-System

3. Required Libraries Install Cheyyandi

pip install -r requirements.txt

4. Application Run Cheyyandi

"app.py" lo use chestunna framework batti application ni run cheyyandi.

For Streamlit:

streamlit run app.py

Browser lo application open ayyaka image/video input ichhi fire detection test cheyyachu.

